        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "e331a98f-fa81-50d5-b36f-ddaa0ab36765",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: The Bassarids, Don Quichotte, Cardillac, Die Jakobsleiter, Melusine\n- People: Hans Werner Henze, W. H. Auden, Chester Kallman, Euripides, Jules Massenet, Henri Caïn, Bodo Igesz, Paul Hindemith, Arnold Schoenberg, Aribert Reimann\n- Organizations: Salzburg Festival, Santa Fe Opera\n- Concepts: opera, libretto, United States premieres\n\nFacts:\n- Don Quichotte is an opera in five acts by Jules Massenet with a French libretto by Henri Caïn.\n- The Bassarids is an opera in one act and an intermezzo with music by Hans Werner Henze.\n- The Bassarids has an English libretto by W. H. Auden and Chester Kallman and is based on Euripides's The Bacchae.\n- Bodo Igesz staged operas for the Salzburg Festival and numerous operas for the Santa Fe Opera.\n- In 1967, Bodo Igesz staged the United States premiere of Hindemith's Cardillac for the Santa Fe Opera.\n- In 1968, Bodo Igesz staged the United States premieres of Schoenberg's Die Jakobsleiter and Henze's The Bassarids for the Santa Fe Opera.\n- In 1972, Bodo Igesz staged the United States premiere of Aribert Reimann's Melusine for the Santa Fe Opera.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
